  "description": "The original Ghisallo was the lightest titanium bike ever made and the envy of riders the world over. Now, it has been brought back to life for a limited run of 15 bikes. Experience history aboard one of Litespeed’s greatest creations. An alpine symphony—the Ghisallo is built specifically for lightweight climbers who live to conquer the highest mountains. It maintains the spirit of the original with classic rim brakes and the original Ghisallo's 3-piece titanium bottom bracket. Limited edition frames stamped 1 through 20 Includes a certificate of authenticity with actual measured frame weight Frame weight: 871 grams (size medium) 6.5 kg / 14 lb 6 oz complete bike weight (size medium) Recommended 85 kg / 187 lb rider weight limit Superform FW 3AL/2.5V titanium tubing Original Ghisallo 3-Piece Welded threaded BSA bottom bracket Maximum tire size: 28mm* Shimano Di2 or SRAM eTap AXS-specific design Proudly handcrafted in Chattanooga, TN, using globally sourced premium materials *Varies based on tire brand, tread, wheel, and fork combination.",
